#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:2
msgid "Terminal-side ink"
msgstr "终端侧墨迹"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:6
msgid ""
"A program that draws with a pen receives a report from the :doc:`tablet-protocol`, appends a "
"point to a pen stroke of a :doc:`vector image <vector-protocol>` and waits for the terminal to "
"draw it. Every sample of the pen therefore travels from the terminal to the program and back "
"before any ink shows, and when the program is at the far end of a network connection the network "
"is crossed twice. The line lags behind the pen, which is the one thing a drawing program cannot "
"afford."
msgstr ""
"使用笔绘图的程序收到 :doc:`tablet-protocol` 报告后，会向 :doc:`矢量图像 <vector-protocol>` "
"的笔划添加一点，再等待终端绘制。因此每个笔采样都必须从终端到程序再返回，墨迹才显示；程序位于网络另一端时，需要两次跨越网络。线条会落后于笔，这正是绘图程序最不能容忍的情况。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:14
msgid ""
"Terminal-side ink lets the terminal draw the stroke itself. The program gives it a brush for one "
"of its vector images, and from then on the terminal adds the points of each stroke to that image "
"as the pen moves, at once, while the reports go to the program as they always did. The terminal "
"draws no overlay of its own: it applies to the image exactly the records the program would have "
"sent, so the stroke is an ordinary element of the program's scene, with an id the program chose, "
"which the program keeps, replaces with a better one or deletes. Nothing else about vector images "
"changes. It is an open terminal extension like the others here: small, unobtrusive, easy to "
"implement, and no change to what the TTY is."
msgstr ""
"终端侧墨迹允许终端自行绘制笔划。程序为某幅矢量图像提供画笔，此后终端随笔移动立即向图像添加各笔划的点，同时仍照常向程序发送报告。终端不绘制独立蒙层，而是向图像应用程序本来会发送的完全相同记录。因此笔划是程序场景中的普通元素，ID"
" 由程序选择，程序可保留、替换为更好的笔划或删除。矢量图像的其他行为不变。它与其他扩展一样，是小巧、低干扰、易于实现的开放终端扩展，不改变 TTY 的本质。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:26
msgid "Framing"
msgstr "消息封装"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:28
msgid "Frames are ``OSC 777`` with the ``ink`` selector::"
msgstr "帧使用带有 ``ink`` 选择器的 ``OSC 777``：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:32
msgid ""
"They follow the rules every OSC 777 extension shares, which :doc:`extension-framing` gives: the "
"syntax of the fields, which frames are rejected, and the units. Values are decimal integers, "
"except the widths and the exponent of a brush, which are numbers as the records of a vector image"
" write them and may have a fraction, and its color. ``v``, the protocol version, is ``1``, and "
"``op`` is one of ``query``, ``cap``, ``brush`` and ``mode``. The terminal sends only replies, "
"which are never merged or dropped."
msgstr ""
"帧遵循 :doc:`extension-framing` 规定的 OSC 777 "
"共用规则：字段语法、拒绝哪些帧，以及单位。除画笔的宽度、指数和颜色外，数值均为十进制整数；宽度和指数遵循矢量记录的数值格式，可带小数。协议版本 ``v`` 为 ``1``，``op`` 为 "
"``query``、``cap``、``brush`` 或 ``mode``。终端仅发送回复，回复绝不合并或丢弃。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:42
msgid "Discovery"
msgstr "能力探测"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:44
msgid "A program asks the terminal whether it can ink::"
msgstr "程序询问终端是否能绘制墨迹：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:48
msgid ""
"``id`` is a non-negative 31 bit integer of the program's choosing, echoed in the reply so replies"
" can be matched to queries. A supporting terminal answers::"
msgstr "``id`` 是程序自行选择的非负 31 位整数，回复原样返回，以便匹配查询。支持协议的终端回答：::"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:54
msgid ""
"``caps`` is a bit set, of which only ``1`` is defined: the terminal draws strokes. ``mode`` is "
"``1`` while ink is on and ``0`` otherwise. When the terminal holds a brush the reply also carries"
" it, with the fields of `The brush`_ as the terminal has them, ``k`` being the id the next stroke"
" will get and ``n`` how many ids are left::"
msgstr ""
"``caps`` 是位集合，目前仅定义 ``1``，表示终端绘制笔划。墨迹启用时 ``mode`` 为 ``1``，否则为 ``0``。终端保存画笔时，回复还携带 `画笔 <The "
"brush_>`_ 规定的当前画笔字段，其中 ``k`` 为下一笔将取得的 ID，``n`` 为剩余 ID 数量：:: #noqa"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:62
msgid ""
"A terminal that does not support the protocol ignores the query, so a program must time out and "
"go on drawing its strokes itself, which it must be able to do in any case. A query changes "
"nothing."
msgstr "不支持本协议的终端会忽略查询，因此程序必须设置超时，并继续自行绘制笔划；无论如何程序都必须具备自行绘制能力。查询不改变状态。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:67
msgid "The brush"
msgstr "画笔"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:69
msgid "A program turns ink on by giving the terminal a brush::"
msgstr "程序通过向终端提供画笔来开启墨迹：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:74
msgid "``i``"
msgstr "``i``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:74
msgid ""
"Required. The id of a vector image (``f=200``) of this window, as the graphics protocol knows it."
" The image need not exist yet; a stroke begins only over an image that does"
msgstr "必需。本窗口中一幅矢量图像（``f=200``）的图形协议 ID。图像可以尚不存在，但只有在已有图像上才能开始笔划"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:77
msgid "``g``"
msgstr "``g``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:77
msgid "The id of the group of that image the strokes go into, ``0``, the root group, by default"
msgstr "笔划所属图像分组的 ID，默认为根分组 ``0``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:79
msgid "``k``"
msgstr "``k``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:79
msgid "Required. The id the element of the first stroke gets, at least ``1``"
msgstr "必需。第一笔对应元素的 ID，至少为 ``1``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:81
msgid "``n``"
msgstr "``n``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:81
msgid ""
"How many ids, counting up from ``k``, the program sets aside for the terminal, ``1`` by default. "
"The last of them may not exceed 4294967295. The program must not use these ids for anything else"
msgstr "程序从 ``k`` 起为终端保留的连续 ID 数量，默认 ``1``。最后一个 ID 不得超过 4294967295。程序不得将这些 ID 用于其他用途"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:84
msgid "``fill``"
msgstr "``fill``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:84
msgid ""
"The color of the strokes, as vector records write a color, ``#rrggbb``, ``#rrggbbaa`` or ``@`` "
"and the id of a gradient. Black by default; ``none`` is refused"
msgstr "笔划颜色，采用矢量记录格式：``#rrggbb``、``#rrggbbaa``，或 ``@`` 后接渐变 ID。默认黑色；拒绝 ``none``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:87
msgid "``w1``"
msgstr "``w1``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:87
msgid ""
"Required. The width of the stroke under full pressure, in the units of the group, a finite number"
" from 0 up"
msgstr "必需。满压力时的笔划宽度，以分组单位表示，为不小于 0 的有限数"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:89
msgid "``w0``"
msgstr "``w0``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:89
msgid "The width under no pressure, the same as ``w1`` by default, which gives a stroke of constant width"
msgstr "无压力时的宽度，默认与 ``w1`` 相同，即固定宽度"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:91
msgid "``e``"
msgstr "``e``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:91
msgid "The exponent of the curve between the two, a finite number greater than 0, ``1`` by default"
msgstr "两个宽度之间压力曲线的指数，必须为大于 0 的有限数，默认 ``1``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:93
msgid "``tools``"
msgstr "``tools``"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:93
msgid ""
"The tools that draw, a bit set with bit ``1 << tool`` for each ``tool`` value of the tablet "
"pointer protocol: pen ``2``, eraser ``4``, brush ``8``, pencil ``16``, airbrush ``32``, mouse "
"``64``, lens ``128``, totem ``256`` and an unknown tool ``1``. By default ``58``, the pen, brush,"
" pencil and airbrush. From 1 to 511"
msgstr ""
"参与绘制的工具位集合，数位板指针协议每个 ``tool`` 值对应位 ``1 << tool``：笔 ``2``、橡皮 ``4``、画笔 ``8``、铅笔 ``16``、喷枪 ``32``、鼠标"
" ``64``、镜头工具 ``128``、图腾工具 ``256``、未知工具 ``1``。默认 ``58``，包括笔、画笔、铅笔和喷枪。范围为 1 至 511"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:100
msgid ""
"A brush replaces the one before it, ids included, and turns ink on. The eraser is left out by "
"default because what erasing means is the program's business; a program that wants the other end "
"of the pen to paint, with the color of its page for instance, gives a brush that says so."
msgstr "新画笔替换旧画笔（含 ID 范围），并开启墨迹。默认不包括橡皮，因为擦除含义由程序定义；若希望笔的另一端也绘制，例如用页面颜色涂抹，可提供包含橡皮的画笔。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:106
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "模式"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:108
msgid "Ink is turned off with::"
msgstr "关闭墨迹：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:112
msgid ""
"The terminal keeps the brush, and ``mode=1`` turns ink on again with it and the ids it has left, "
"so a program can stop the terminal drawing while its own eraser or selection tool is in use and "
"start it again without sending the brush. ``mode=1`` does nothing when there is no brush. A "
"``mode`` request without a ``mode`` field reads the state and is answered with::"
msgstr ""
"终端保留画笔，``mode=1`` 可用其剩余 ID 重新启用。因此程序在使用自己的橡皮或选择工具时可暂时停止终端绘制，之后无须重传画笔即可恢复。没有画笔时，``mode=1`` "
"不产生效果。不带 ``mode`` 字段的 ``mode`` 请求读取状态，回复为：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:120
msgid ""
"The mode and the brush are local to the window. ``RIS`` turns ink off and forgets the brush. "
"Programs must turn ink off when they exit, suspend or fail, and give the brush again when "
"resumed; a program resuming after a reconnection queries to learn what survived rather than "
"assuming. A terminal may let its user refuse ink, for every program or for some. A refused mode "
"reads back as off and nothing is drawn, so a program reads the mode back rather than assume it "
"was granted."
msgstr ""
"模式和画笔均局限于当前窗口。``RIS`` "
"关闭墨迹并清除画笔。程序必须在退出、挂起或失败时关闭墨迹，恢复时重新提供画笔；重连后应通过查询确认保留了什么，不要假定状态仍在。终端可允许用户针对全部或部分程序拒绝墨迹。被拒绝时读回为关闭且不绘制，因此程序应读回模式，不要假定已获准。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:128
msgid ""
"Ink needs the reports of tools: the window must have bit ``1`` of the mode of the :doc:`tablet-"
"protocol` on. Without it a pen is a mouse, there are no strokes and nothing is drawn. A program "
"that never sends a brush sees no difference at all."
msgstr "墨迹依赖工具报告：窗口必须开启 :doc:`tablet-protocol` 模式的位 ``1``。否则笔作为鼠标使用，没有笔划，也不绘制。未发送画笔的程序完全不受影响。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:134
msgid "Strokes"
msgstr "笔划"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:136
msgid ""
"While ink is on, a stroke of the tablet pointer protocol, from the ``down`` of a tool to its "
"``up``, becomes a stroke of ink when"
msgstr "墨迹启用期间，从工具 ``down`` 到 ``up`` 的数位板指针笔划，在满足以下条件时转为墨迹笔划："

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:139
msgid "the tool is one of those the brush names,"
msgstr "工具在画笔指定的集合中；"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:140
msgid ""
"the ``down`` is over a placement of the image, and, when several placements of it are under the "
"pen, over the one drawn on top of the others: the one with the highest ``z``, and among equals "
"the one placed last,"
msgstr "``down`` 位于目标图像的一次放置上；若笔下有同一图像的多次放置，则选择最上层，即 ``z`` 最大、相同 ``z`` 时最后放置的那个；"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:144
msgid "the group exists, is a group, and the transforms from the root group down to it can be inverted,"
msgstr "目标分组存在且确为分组，从根分组到目标分组的所有变换均可逆；"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:146
msgid ""
"an id is left, and the terminal has room for another stroke; a terminal may limit how many tools "
"it draws for at once."
msgstr "还有剩余 ID，且终端有空间容纳新笔划；终端可能限制同时为多少个工具绘制。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:149
msgid ""
"Then the terminal applies to the image, exactly as if the program had sent it with the edit "
"action of the vector format, the record::"
msgstr "随后终端向图像应用以下记录，效果与程序通过矢量格式编辑操作发送该记录完全相同：::"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:154
msgid ""
"with the point the ``down`` report gives, see `From a report to a point`_, and uses up that id. "
"The report of the ``down`` that the program receives carries one more field, ``ink``, with the id"
" of the element::"
msgstr ""
"使用 ``down`` 报告给出的点（见 `从报告换算到点 <From a report to a point_>`_），并消耗该 ID。程序收到的 ``down`` 报告会额外带有 "
"``ink`` 字段，值为元素 ID：:: #noqa"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:160
msgid "Every later report of that stroke, each ``move`` and the ``up``, appends the point it gives::"
msgstr "该笔划后续的每次 ``move`` 和最终 ``up`` 都会追加相应的点：::"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:165
msgid ""
"The ``up`` ends the stroke. A ``down`` without an ``ink`` field began a stroke the terminal is "
"not drawing, whatever the reason, and the program draws it itself as it would without this "
"protocol. That is also how a program learns that the ids have run out: it gives a brush with "
"more."
msgstr ""
"``up`` 结束笔划。不带 ``ink`` 字段的 ``down`` 表示终端因某种原因未绘制此笔划；程序应像不支持本协议时一样自行绘制。ID 耗尽时程序也通过这种方式得知，并可提供带有更多 "
"ID 的新画笔。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:170
msgid ""
"The element is the program's from the moment it exists. Usually the program leaves it as it is. "
"It may replace it, with a ``k`` record of the same id, by a stroke it has smoothed or thinned, or"
" delete it with an ``x`` record, and should do either after the ``up``: a record that replaces "
"the element while the stroke is being drawn is followed by the points the terminal goes on "
"appending to whatever has that id."
msgstr ""
"元素自创建起就属于程序。通常程序原样保留；也可在 ``up`` 之后，用相同 ID 的 ``k`` 记录替换为平滑或简化后的笔划，或用 ``x`` "
"记录删除。如果在绘制期间替换元素，终端仍会继续向占用该 ID 的对象追加后续点。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:177
msgid ""
"A stroke that the tablet pointer protocol cancels, with ``phase=4``, never happened: the terminal"
" deletes its element, as the record ``x id=<that id>`` does, before it sends the report of the "
"cancel. The id is not given again."
msgstr "数位板指针协议通过 ``phase=4`` 取消的笔划视为从未发生：终端在发送取消报告前删除元素，等同于 ``x id=<that id>``。该 ID 不会重新使用。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:181
msgid "Reports of hovering draw nothing, and fingers are not inked."
msgstr "悬停报告不绘制，手指也不产生墨迹。"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:184
msgid "From a report to a point"
msgstr "从报告换算到点"

#: docs/ink-protocol.rst:186
msgid ""
"The point a report adds is worked out from the report alone and from what the terminal is showing"
" when it makes the report, so that a program, or a relay that mirrors the scene, arrives at the "
"same numbers. They are real numbers, computed in double precision; a difference in the last digit"
" is of no account."
msgstr "添加的点仅根据报告及终端生成报告时所显示的状态计算，因此程序或镜像场景的中继可以算出相同结果。结果是双精度实数，末位数字差异无需考虑。"

